  "word_count": 129,
  "text_content": "Ada and Tunde planted maize in the school garden. Every morning, they carried water from the tap in a bucket. After two weeks, tiny green shoots appeared in the dark soil. One afternoon, a hungry goat pushed through the fence and chewed the leaves. Tunde was upset, but Ada quickly thought of a plan. They asked their teacher for spare sticks and some rope. Together they mended the fence until it was strong and tall. The goat returned the next morning, but it could not get through. By the end of term, the maize had grown taller than Tunde. The children harvested the cobs and roasted them with Mama. Everyone in the class enjoyed a sweet, smoky piece. Tunde smiled and promised to build the fence first next time.",
